[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Vienna Game"]
[Variation "Vienna Game: Vienna Gambit, Breyer Variation"]
[ECO "C29"]
[Character "gambit,sharp"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "centre-fight,development-lead"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "main"]
[Opponent "3...d5"]
[Start "vienna-gambit 4.fxe5"]

4... Nxe4 { Takes the pawn back, and the knight attacks c3 and the pawn on d2. The centre is now Black's. } ( 4... Ng4 5. d4 { Takes the centre and keeps the g4 knight out of play; after ...dxe4 Nxe4 White is a pawn up. } 5... dxe4 6. Nxe4 ) ( 4... Nc6 5. exf6 { Wins a whole knight: the one on f6 is attacked and Black's reply cannot save it. } 5... dxe4 6. Nxe4 ) 5. Nf3 { Develops a piece and stops ...Qh4+. If Black takes on c3, White recaptures with a pawn and keeps building, so the knight need not be saved. } 5... Be7 ( 5... Nc6 6. Bb5 { Pins the knight to the king's side of the board, adds pressure on the e4 knight and gets ready to castle. } 6... Be7 7. Qe2 ) ( 5... Bg4 6. Qe2 { Hits the knight on e4 down the e-file, so Black has to deal with that first. } 6... Nxc3 7. dxc3 ) 6. d4 { Grabs the centre and opens the bishop on c1. The pawn on d4 is the base of everything White does here. } 6... O-O ( 6... c5 7. Bd3 { Develops, hits the knight on e4 and heads for castling. } 7... Nxc3 8. bxc3 c4 9. Be2 ) 7. Bd3 { Hits the knight on e4 and clears the way to castle. If Black takes on c3 White recaptures with the b-pawn. } 7... f5 { Supports the centre knight and breaks open the position. } ( 7... Nxc3 8. bxc3 { Recaptures with the b-pawn so the pawn on d4 stays in the centre. } 8... c5 9. O-O ) 8. exf6 { Takes the f5 pawn as it passes (en passant). Leaving the pawn on f5 would give Black a solid wall of pawns and a safe knight on e4. } 8... Bxf6 9. O-O { Castles so the king is safe before the position opens, and the rook is already on the f-file. } 9... Nc6 ( 9... Nxc3 10. bxc3 Nc6 11. Qe1 { Brings the queen towards the king side and the open file. } 11... Be7 12. Rb1 ) 10. Nxe4 { Swaps off Black's best piece, the knight that has been sitting on e4. } 10... dxe4 11. Bxe4 { Wins the pawn back and puts the bishop on a long diagonal aiming at h7. Plan: bring the queen out with Qh5 or Qd3, and keep the f-file busy. If the position opens, trade pieces and enjoy the lead in development. } *
